For those who seem puzzled about it:

There is just one NetHack 3.0 development team.  It's membership is
listed in your 'history' file.

In the last few weeks three new auxiliary teams were created:  A PC
overlay team, a Mac team, and an Amiga team.  These auxiliary teams
are composed of volunteers knowledgable in the machines in question
plus a few members of the development team (mainly for coordinating
purposes).  The membership of these auxiliary teams will be listed
in the updated 'history' file once Patch 7 is released.  The main
purpose of these auxiliary teams is to update and enhance the
respective NetHack 3.0 ports.

The address of the development team AND the auxiliary teams is the
same: nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu.  If you wish to address
directly one of the auxiliary teams, specify this on the 'Subject'
line of your msg.  But nethack-bugs msgs always get sorted out, and
they are re-directed (if necessary) to those among us in a position 
to provide a most useful response.

This burst of activity by the development team and its auxiliaries is
in preparation for Patch 7 which (as was stated a number of times) is
intended to be the last NetHack 3.0 official patch.  It is in line
with our aim to leave behind as bugfree and portable a version of 3.0
as possible.

For the development team,

-Izchak
 


